Then why should a user interact with datalad as an additional dependency?\n - If I use datalad, and datalad eventually goes away, do I still get power to use git-annex? What do I lose? \n\n## What is a superdataset\nThe core of this question is:\n\n\u003e How does Github relate to DataLad?\n\nDatalad (if I understand correctly) defines a superdataset as a collection of datasets, where each dataset is a folder with an annex in a github repository. It seems like this means we have one upper level git folder, and then each subfolder (a submodle?) has had the git-annex init called within. \n\n - This means that Github is being used for version control of git annex?\n -  There is no \"Github equivalent for just Git Annex\" outside of this? \n - If a user doesn't have datalad, how would a git-annex be shared or otherwise version controlled?\n - I want to understand how the [Github repository here](https://github.com/datalad/datasets.datalad.org) relates to files on some local machine, some storage, and then the [web interface here](http://datasets.datalad.org/?dir=/adhd200/RawDataBIDS/NeuroIMAGE). I want to understand this enough so I can answer the question **how do I create my own superdataset?**\n\nI did find datalad on the list of public repositories page (https://git-annex.branchable.com/publicrepos/) that somewhat suggested this last idea! \n\nSo looking at the Github repository for datalad superdataset, I see a bunch of folders with submodules to other folders, and a .datalad file and a bunch of meta.json (I think to describe the metadata for each linked folder?) Does this mean that the git-annex part is still not represented here, but used in some way by datalab to parse and then obtain the annex? What I don't understand is how this repository turns into the datalab portal where I can click through datasets. The underlying questions are \"How do I make this myself\" and \"how much of this is relying on datalab, vs, is just git annex?\" and \"how is git really involved aside from storing metadata about datalad?","files":null}]}